From 23feee119a3e54e3c6e7af58fc3d6ab54a8a0fd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Ferreira <gabrielcarvfer@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] lkl: update jiffies on interrupts while the tick is stopped

irq_enter() brings a stale jiffies up to date (tick_irq_enter) only
when the idle task is current. LKL idles in idle_host_task, a regular
task, or in a host task that stays current after a system call, so the
interrupts taken while the tick is stopped (see "lkl: stop the tick
while the host is idle") ran with an old jiffies. The timers armed from
them, such as the TCP retransmission timer armed on an incoming ACK,
expired early by the time elapsed since the tick stopped, which caused
spurious retransmissions: in ns-3 DCE, a transfer losing 10 segments
retransmitted 84.

Update jiffies as the idle task would when an interrupt starts while
another task is current.
---
 arch/lkl/kernel/irq.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/lkl/kernel/irq.c b/arch/lkl/kernel/irq.c
index 54c5686ab..dca9dc1af 100644
--- a/arch/lkl/kernel/irq.c
+++ b/arch/lkl/kernel/irq.c
@@ -61,6 +61,14 @@ static void run_irq(int irq)
 	/* interrupt handlers need to run with interrupts disabled */
 	local_irq_save(flags);
 	irq_enter();
+	/*
+	 * irq_enter() brings a stale jiffies up to date only when the idle
+	 * task is current, but LKL idles in idle_host_task or in a host
+	 * task: without this, handlers running while the tick is stopped
+	 * see an old jiffies and arm their timers too early.
+	 */
+	if (!is_idle_task(current) && irq_count() == HARDIRQ_OFFSET)
+		tick_irq_enter();
 	generic_handle_irq(irq);
 	irq_exit();
 	set_irq_regs(old_regs);
-- 
